    <statement><p>Evaluate the integral
<me>\int {\frac{6}{(x+a)(x+b)}}\, dx</me>
for the cases where <m>a=b</m> and where <m>a \ne b.</m></p>
<p>Note:  For the case where <m>a=b,</m> use only <m>a</m> in your answer.  Also, use an upper-case "C" for the constant of integration.</p>
<p>If <m>a=b:</m>  <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>If <m>a \ne b:</m>  <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6\frac{-1}{x+a}+C+c</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{6}{b-a}\ln\mathopen{}\left(\left|\frac{x+a}{x+b}\right|\right)+C+c</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
